      AppSettings:AdminUserPhoneNumber cannot name an account: it is empty or holds characters outside the set Identity allows in an account name (+0123456789), so the lookup can never match and NOBODY will ever hold PowerUserRole in this deployment. Every [Authorize(Roles = PowerUserRole)] endpoint refuses every caller and StoreAdminPolicy admits store admins only. Committed appsettings.json ships the "Set in Azure" placeholder, so an environment that does not override the value lands here: set it in Azure configuration or user secrets to the administrator's phone number in the exact form the account is registered with.
